  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Huang Jin Immortal Gu Houses gather above Blood Plain as eleven Huang Jin tribes answer the call, including Nu Er tribe with Loud Thunder Hall, Gong tribe with Golden Dawn Hall, and Yao tribe with Divine Light Hall. Nu Er Qian warns Nu Er Gu not to stand out, naming Yao tribe, Guan tribe, and Liu tribe as the ones nearer to Chu Sect and Bai Zu tribe, and saying that overexertion would only let others reap the benefits.",
      "chapters": [
        1193
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_immortal_gu_house",
        "loc_blood_plain",
        "fac_huang_jin_bloodline",
        "fac_nu_er_tribe",
        "house_loud_thunder_hall",
        "fac_gong_tribe",
        "house_golden_dawn_hall",
        "fac_yao_tribe",
        "char_nu_er_qian",
        "char_nu_er_gu",
        "fac_guan_tribe",
        "fac_liu_tribe",
        "fac_chu_sect",
        "fac_bai_zu_tribe"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Yao Huang was friends with Heavenly Lord Bai Zu, so he came up with the blood battle martial competition as an explanation to Longevity Heaven while his main focus stayed on refining Gu. Yao tribe sent the healing Gu Immortal Yao Yuan Ying, and some combative Yao tribe Gu Immortals could only grit their teeth under that restraint. Gong tribe, still recovering prestige after the battle at Iron Eagle blessed land, sent Gong Wan Ting instead of Prince Feng Xian. Hei tribe Gu Immortals had already been annexed by Bai Zu tribe and were no longer acknowledged among the Huang Jin tribes.",
      "chapters": [
        1193
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "why-yao-huang-arranged-it",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_yao_huang",
        "char_heavenly_lord_bai_zu",
        "fac_longevity_heaven",
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "char_yao_yuan_ying",
        "loc_iron_eagle_blessed_land",
        "char_gong_wan_ting",
        "char_prince_feng_xian",
        "fac_hei_tribe"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Young Gu Immortals such as Ye Lui Xiao Jin treat the contest as a way to establish their names, and the first battle unfolds under both sides’ gazes. Fang Yuan, still distant from the field, plans to participate a few times, kill Gu Immortals, and seize immortal apertures as a step toward rank seven, while continuing to refine dream path mortal Gu.",
      "chapters": [
        1194
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "opening-fights",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_ye_lui_xiao_jin",
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "sys_dream_path_mortal_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Chu Sect does not stop a victor from taking a corpse, because that is one of the rules stated in the competition agreement, as when Xue Wu Hen stored Liu Hui’s corpse and when Nian Er Ping Zhi took Granny Yin’s body with its immortal aperture. Fang Yuan’s Chu Sect alliance agreement is lenient enough that even if Chu Sect were annihilated he could choose not to appear. He delays joining until he can raise his cultivation to rank seven.",
      "chapters": [
        1196
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "spoils-and-agreement",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_xue_wu_hen",
        "char_liu_hui",
        "char_nian_er_ping_zhi",
        "char_granny_yin"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Most members on Chu Sect and Bai Zu tribe’s side are lone immortals or demonic cultivators, held together by the reputations of Domination Immortal and Heavenly Lord Bai Zu plus the rewards, so Chu Du agrees to exchange corpses in order to stabilize their mindsets for later battles. After that exchange, Gong Wan Ting also negotiates with Chu Du, and both sides conveniently add a rule regarding the exchange of corpses and soul captives. Chu Du has instructions from Heavenly Lord Bai Zu to protect as many Bai Zu tribe descendants as possible, so actual Bai Zu bloodline members are still being taken care of while other fighters are sent out.",
      "chapters": [
        1197
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "corpse-and-soul-exchanges",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_chu_du"
      ]
    }
  ],
